<Base title="Privacy — StreamSnipe"><div class="wrap"><article class="prose"><div class="eyebrow">Your data / Privacy</div><h1>Local is the point.</h1><p class="lead">Your recordings stay with your companion unless you choose to upload them to your own storage.</p><h2>How the studio connects</h2><p>The dashboard connects directly to your local companion. Pairing credentials are stored in your browser for this origin and device. The hosted portal does not receive your recordings, local paths, or S3 credentials.</p><h2>Optional storage</h2><p>If you configure S3-compatible storage, the companion sends uploads directly to the storage service you choose. That provider’s terms and privacy practices apply.</p><h2>Control your access</h2><p>Review or revoke paired sessions in the studio settings. Clearing browser storage removes the local pairing credential from that browser.</p></article></div></Base>
